# Copy this file to `.env` to change a setting. `.env` is git-ignored; this file is not.
#
# Only variables whose name starts with EXPO_PUBLIC_ reach the app. Expo reads them when Metro
# starts, so restart it (npm start -- --clear) after changing one. Never put a secret here: whatever
# starts with EXPO_PUBLIC_ is readable in the bundle.

# How the app is wired (see "Composition root" in the README).
#   mock  The in-memory adapters and a simulated server. Needs no network.
#   http  The real adapters: the HTTP API, the encrypted SQLite database, the secure storage. Needs
#         EXPO_PUBLIC_BOARDROOM_API_BASE_URL below.
# A missing or empty value means mock in a development build, and is an error in any other build
# (missingAdaptersSetting): a release build must be told what it talks to. Any other value is
# refused at start.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BOARDROOM_ADAPTERS=mock

# Where the API is, for the http adapters (see "Running against the mock API" in the README). It is
# an https address, or an http one for this machine only (localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1] and 10.0.2.2,
# which is how the Android emulator reaches the computer it runs on). A development build also
# accepts http for another computer of the network, to reach `npm run mock:api` from a phone: use
# its address, such as http://192.168.1.20:4000. Not used by mock.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BOARDROOM_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000

# The address (DSN) of the Sentry project that receives the crash reports and the error events
# (see "Monitoring: Sentry behind the port" in the README). Empty means off: the events are written to the console. It is
# public by design (it only lets a client send events), which is why it may be an EXPO_PUBLIC_
# variable; the token that uploads the source maps is not, and is never written in a file.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# Build-time settings, for `app.config.ts` and the build tools. They never reach the app, and none
# of them is needed to run it. Set them in the shell, in the secrets of the CI or in the
# environment variables of EAS (see "CI/CD" in the README), not here, except for the first two when
# you publish updates from this machine.
#   EAS_PROJECT_ID      The id of the EAS project: where the app looks for its updates. Without it,
#                       the updates are off in the build.
#   SENTRY_ORG          The Sentry organisation and project that receive the source maps. Together
#   SENTRY_PROJECT      with SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN, they turn the upload on; without the three, the
#   SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN   build does not touch Sentry. The token is a secret: never put it in a file.
#   SENTRY_URL          The Sentry server, for an organisation that is not on https://sentry.io.
#   BOARDROOM_BUILD_NUMBER  The build number of the store build (a positive integer), for the Fastlane
#                       lanes, which number the builds themselves. EAS numbers them remotely.
